        "prototype_units": "meters",
        "ho_scale_units": "millimeters",
        "notes": "Anchorage envelope, 237 ft long by 182 ft wide by 135 ft tall, all sourced (CTL-034/035/036), retiring OQ-008. Extends outboard from the cable point. Drawn in three segments -- either side of the thoroughfare arch and above its crown -- so the street opening registered by CTL-052 is a real void rather than a shape buried inside a solid block. The envelope and its sourced extent are unchanged; only the subdivision differs. Deliberately does NOT cite the arch placeholders: this part's three dimensions are all grade A/B, and the weakest-link rule would otherwise drag a fully sourced envelope down to D because of where a doorway was cut in it. The arch itself carries those references, and its own grade. The Cherry Street and Water Street arches are not separately modelled.",
